# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Zola output
site/public/

.DS_Store

# ── Internal notes, feature specifications and third-party sources ─────────────

# Architecture notes (not published): the D/R/ERR-numbered decisions, risks and
# errata, and ROADMAP.md, the spec of specs — every open item names its feature
# specification.
#
# The OCA specification corpus — the OCPP 1.6, 2.0.1 and 2.1 PDFs, their text
# renderings and errata — lives at `concepts/reference/` and is covered by this
# line: OCA-licensed and not redistributable, indexed with retrieval URLs in
# `concepts/REFERENCES.md`. Only the JSON schemas are vendored, into schemas/.
/concepts/

# This project's own feature specifications, and the Spec Kit machinery that
# produces them: one `specs/NNN-slug/` per ROADMAP item (spec, plan, research,
# tasks), `.specify/memory/constitution.md`, and the `/speckit-*` skills. Same
# rule as `concepts/` — internal, and the published tree may not cite a path its
# reader does not have; `scripts/concepts-check.sh` fails on one that does.
#
# Until 2026-11-07 `specs/` held the OCA corpus now under `concepts/reference/`;
# a stale copy is ignored by the same line. Matches billing, sepa and agentplane.
/specs/
/.specify/
/.claude/
